WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.875
You begin with identity, because
everything else decides on it.

2
00:00:03.875 --> 00:00:09.731
Access policy, devices, data, certificates:
each one asks who or what is making the

3
00:00:09.731 --> 00:00:15.675
request, and that includes service accounts,
applications, devices and AI agents.

4
00:00:15.675 --> 00:00:21.457
Federal identity guidance, OMB memorandum
M-19-17, says those non-person

5
00:00:21.457 --> 00:00:26.275
entities must be distinguishable,
auditable, and consistently managed.

6
00:00:26.275 --> 00:00:29.004
If the answer to that
question isn't trustworthy,

7
00:00:29.004 --> 00:00:31.187
nothing built on top of it can be either.

8
00:00:31.187 --> 00:00:35.732
That's why the workbook numbers its
books in this order, with identity first

9
00:00:35.732 --> 00:00:40.350
and infrastructure next, then the cloud
boundary, assurance and operations.

10
00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.187
Infrastructure sits in the same chain:

11
00:00:43.187 --> 00:00:48.063
if DNS stays integrated with Active
Directory, AD can never retire.

12
00:00:48.063 --> 00:00:50.437
Skipping ahead only moves the problem.

13
00:00:50.437 --> 00:00:54.530
And right now there's an unusual
opportunity on the identity side.
